15	Display.Conversation	Orrin_Ghost	It's gone. I can feel the sky again, every star of it.\Here: my chart. Rook will know what to do with it. Not that it'll steer him anywhere alone: every mark on it is set by the Lodestar, and that was never mine. Its shrine is up in the Rime, by the lake. There's a surveyors' lodge at Frostwatch: they'll point you to it.\And listen, heir. When the Shards were in my eyes I saw the dragon, over the mountains, plain as I see you. It isn't sleeping, whatever they say in the pass. It's eating. And a sword that's slept as long as the one you're after cuts like a stick.	I'll remember.	16
